|     Record current game plan + add higher Brouwer ordinals (Approach H prep)
|     
|     User has ruled the existing oracle-based sandbox candidates "too close
|     to violating the don't-be-lazy rule" of upstream README.md.  No
|     submission is planned; the focus is now on generating ideas and
|     exploring fresh-engine directions whose definitions do NOT reference
|     largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth or anything definitionally tied to
|     contender_5's machinery.
|     
|     This commit:
|     
|     * Adds a "Current Game Plan" section to AGENTS.md immediately after
|       "Next-Contender Ideas".  Documents the don't-be-lazy interpretation,
|       the no-submission rule for this brainstorming relay, and a ranked
|       list of fresh-engine directions to push next.
|     
|     * Stands up sandbox/BrouwerHigh.v: extends sandbox/Brouwer.v with
|       Brouwer-ordinal terms past epsilon_0.  Defines next_epsilon,
|       epsilon_at (for any finite k), epsilon_omega, phi_2, zeta_0, and
|       Gamma_0 (the Feferman-Schutte ordinal).  Companion BigGrow_eN,
|       BigGrow_e_omega, BigGrow_zeta_0, BigGrow_Gamma_0 are total Coq
|       functions nat -> nat with no axioms.  All nine Print Assumptions
|       lines report closed global contexts; coqchk accepts the module;
|       compile time ~1 s.
|     
|     * Adds five new approach sections to IDEAS.md:
|       - Approach G: Conway chained-arrow notation.
|       - Approach H: Veblen and beyond, via Brouwer notations.  Documents
|         the small/large Veblen and Bachmann-Howard ordinal landmarks.
|       - Approach I: Combinatorial growth (TREE, SCG, WORM).
|       - Approach J: A fresh strict-bound connector lemma.  Sketches the
|         Tait/Girard-style reducibility proof structure that would unblock
|         a clean BigGrow-only contender.  Estimated cost 200-500 lines.
|       - Approach K: A "depth-bounded max over Brouwer-FGH-typed terms"
|         language, replacing STLC+NatRec with a Brouwer-ordinal-typed
|         alternative.
|       - Approach L: Iteration / composition of fresh combinators
|         (BigGrow, Hardy at higher ordinals, Goodstein) without language
|         extension.
|     
|     The connector lemma (Approach J) is identified as the most direct
|     route to a fresh-engine contender_6 := BigGrow N.  All other approaches
|     either need substantial encoding work (System F, Goodstein, TREE) or
|     hit the same connector-lemma question in a different language.
|     
