| 
|     Add BigGrow + R_tower combination sandbox (composing two axes)
|     
|     New sandbox file: sandbox/BigGrowRTower.v.
|     
|     The previous sandbox/BigGrowPrevMax.v uses the existing Brouwer-FGH
|     (BigGrow := FGH epsilon_0) plus a tPrevMax oracle, and instantiates
|     the oracle to Contender.largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth.  But the
|     generic step lemma prevMax_lt_BGPrev is parameterized over any oracle,
|     so we can plug in stronger oracles -- in particular R_tower 1 from the
|     reflection track -- and inherit their strength for free.
|     
|     Three flavors, all axiom-free:
|     
|     * contender_BG_RT_simple := BigGrow (S (R_tower 1 45)).
|       Pure function composition; no depth-bounded enumeration involved.
|     
|     * contender_BG_RT_layered := largest_BGPrev_nat_of_depth (R_tower 1) 49.
|       Same depth-bounded reflective machinery as BigGrowPrevMax.v, with
|       R_tower 1 plugged in as the prevMax oracle.
|     
|     * contender_BG_RT_stacked := BigGrow (S contender_BG_RT_layered).
|       Stacks BigGrow on top of the layered version using BigGrow_ge.
|     
|     All four chain: contender_5 < R_tower 1 45 < contender_BG_RT_layered
|     < contender_BG_RT_stacked, plus contender_5 < contender_BG_RT_simple
|     via BigGrow_ge.  All Print Assumptions report closed global contexts.
|     
|     This is the first concrete artifact that *composes* impredicative
|     reflection (Approach D.1) and ordinal-indexed FGH growth (Approach A
|     via Brouwer ordinals) in a single contender, mechanically beating
|     contender_5 without needing any proof-theoretic-ordinal-of-System-T
|     meta-theorem.
|     
|     The proven *lower bound* on values is still mild (only +1 from S /
|     BigGrow_ge), but the actual *values* are enormously larger; sharper
|     proven bounds would require additional properties of BigGrow
|     (e.g. BigGrow x >= 2x, BigGrow x >= x^2) which are true but not
|     currently proved.
|     
|     IDEAS.md and AGENTS.md updated.
|     
