* commit be517ee0f2d10bfe4f9e4234a11731ab62521237
| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Thu Apr 30 17:18:23 2026 -0700
| 
|     Add Brouwer-ordinal FGH sandbox (bypass Approach A's Acc obstacle)
|     
|     New sandbox file: sandbox/Brouwer.v.
|     
|     The original Approach A path (sandbox/FGH.v) represents ordinals in
|     Cantor Normal Form and uses a fuel parameter for FGH because the open
|     problem is well-foundedness of the canonical CNF ordering.  This file
|     side-steps that problem by switching to Brouwer ordinal notations:
|     
|         Inductive Brouwer :=
|         | Bz   : Brouwer
|         | Bsucc: Brouwer -> Brouwer
|         | Blim : (nat -> Brouwer) -> Brouwer.
|     
|     In Brouwer notations each limit ordinal carries its fundamental
|     sequence as data, and Coq's W-type structural-subterm rule accepts a
|     [Fixpoint] recursive call on [f n] inside the [Blim f] case.  So
|     [FGH], [Hardy], [Badd], [Bmul], [omega_pow], and [epsilon_0] all live
|     as plain [Fixpoint]s -- no [Acc], no [Fix], no fuel.
|     
|     Concretely the file delivers:
|     
|     * The Brouwer type and basic ordinals (omega, omega_omega, omega^^n,
|       epsilon_0).
|     * Total Brouwer ordinal addition, multiplication, and omega-exp.
|     * Fast-growing hierarchy [FGH : Brouwer -> nat -> nat] and
|       Hardy hierarchy [Hardy : Brouwer -> nat -> nat].
|     * [BigGrow := FGH epsilon_0 : nat -> nat], a total Coq function
|       that dominates every primitive-recursive function.
|     * Small structural lemmas (FGH_Bsucc / FGH_Blim / FGH_one_eq /
|       Nat_iter_FGH_Bz, plus Hardy analogues) for downstream use.
|     * Sanity checks at small ordinals, all matching the FGH textbook:
|       f_2(4) = 64, f_3(2) = 2048, f_omega(2) = 8, etc.
|     
|     Print Assumptions for FGH/Hardy/epsilon_0/BigGrow all close under
|     the global context.  coqchk accepts the module.  Compile time ~1 s.
|     
|     Open follow-up (the only remaining gate for Approach A or a
|     Brouwer-based Approach E contender): prove BigGrow 42 > contender_5
|     via a meta-theorem bounding STLC+NatRec evals at depth 42 by f_alpha(42)
|     for some alpha < epsilon_0.  That is the proof-theoretic ordinal of
|     System T -- true and well-known, but a substantial Coq formalization.
|     
|     IDEAS.md state-of-play and Track 2 recommendation updated.  AGENTS.md
|     sandbox listing updated.
|     
|     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
| 
