|     Add d-monotonicity lemmas to ReflectTowerNoAx (Phase 2 prerequisite)
|     
|     Three new lemmas in sandbox/ReflectTowerNoAx.v:
|     
|     * maxBy_eq_or_in -- the result of maxBy is either the initial best or
|       an element of the list.  Standard accessory.
|     * maxBy_subset -- list-monotonicity of maxBy: enlarging the input list
|       (sublist condition) only increases f (maxBy f m b _).  Proven via a
|       case split on maxBy_eq_or_in plus maxBy_at_least_currentMax /
|       lowerbound_maxBy.
|     * largest_reflect_d_mono -- depth-monotonicity of
|       largest_reflect_nat_of_depth: at fixed prevMax, monotone in d.  Direct
|       consequence of maxBy_subset and termsUpTo_correct.
|     * R_tower_S_d_mono -- depth-monotonicity of R_tower at any positive
|       level.  The level-0 case is deliberately skipped to keep
|       Contender.largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth Opaque (so the kernel
|       cannot try to unfold the depth-42 enumeration).
|     
|     These unblock "Phase 2" of IDEAS.md Approach D.2: a witness with
|     computed-via-NatRec K and/or D values can pad D to any value beyond
|     the chain lemma's exact 3K+42 by composing R_tower_S_d_mono with
|     R_tower_step.
|     
|     Print Assumptions still reports closed under the global context for
|     both contender_5_lt_reflect_tower_7 (now in ReflectTowerNoAx.v) and
|     the downstream contender_5_lt_reflect_rtower_small.  Compile time
|     ~3 s on this machine.
|     
