* commit d1ed169a164b676161d2c5b2ef79f983f497fa1f
| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Thu Apr 30 09:02:05 2026 -0700
| 
|     Add ReflectTower sandbox: stratified reflection tower (Approach D.1)
|     
|     Generalises sandbox/ReflectPrev.v from a one-level reflective extension
|     of STLC+NatRec to the parameterised tower
|     
|       R_tower 0 d     := largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth d
|       R_tower (S k) d := largest depth-d value in STLC+NatRec + tPrevMax
|                          with tPrevMax interpreted as R_tower k.
|     
|     A single uniform witness (S (tPrevMax (natlit d))) at each level gives
|     the level-step lemma R_tower k d < R_tower (S k) (d + 3), which iterates
|     to R_tower 0 42 < R_tower (S n) (3*(S n) + 42) for any n. The file
|     materialises the case n = 99, depth 342, and proves
|     contender_5 < R_tower 100 342 in ~3.5 s of compile time.
|     
|     Engineering note: requires Opaque pragmas on
|     Contender.largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth and on the new
|     largest_reflect_nat_of_depth / eval / termsUpTo / maxBy after their
|     structural lemmas, otherwise the kernel's conversion check tries to
|     fully enumerate depth-D STLC+NatRec terms when unifying R_tower (S k) D
|     with the lemma conclusion, and never returns. IDEAS.md records the
|     mechanism and the lesson.
|     
|     Print Assumptions reports only functional_extensionality_dep, used by
|     the standard reduction-lemma machinery for the typed evaluator (the same
|     axiom Contender.v's reification helpers use). A no-axioms refactor is
|     listed as Track 1 of the recommendation in IDEAS.md.
|     
|     IDEAS.md additionally adds an Approach D.2 sketch (primitivising R_tower
|     itself as tRTower in a new reflective language) and rewrites the
|     Recommendation section around three concrete tracks.
|     
|     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
| 
